{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-342498" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}2x+3, & x\\in [-3,0) \\\\ (x-3)^{2}-3, & x\\in [0,3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe above function $F(x)$ is defined on $x\\in [-3,3).$ Let $f(x)$ be the $6$-periodic extension of $F(x)$ to $x\\in R.$\nSelect the correct options below.\n\n| I. | $F(x)$ is continuous on $x\\in (-3,3)$ | {{field-1}} |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| II. | $F(x)$ is piecewise smooth on $x\\in (-3,3)$ | {{field-2}} |\n| III. | ${lim}_{x\\to -{3}^{+}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to {3}^{-}}F(x)$ | {{field-3}} |\n| IV. | $f(x)$ is piecewise smooth and continuous on $R$ | {{field-4}} |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069003/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e0ef6d55925293a63fd3c25a7345dea904c95e009d8872ee551c3b5128c1c58"} {"question" "q-342498" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's examine the given statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is $\\text{false}.$ The function $F(x)$ has a jump discontinuity at $x=0.$ Its graph is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069003/assets/385029e7709a8d4eda45b101aba6f553c79ae3baef5b97080844e307a0b71cc7.png)\n\n- Statement II is $\\text{true}.$ The function $F(x)$ is piecewise smooth on $x\\in (-3,3).$ It consists of two smooth pieces.\n\n- Statement III is $\\text{true}.$ Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -{3}^{+}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to -{3}^{+}}(2x+3)=2(-3)+3=-3\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {3}^{-}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to {3}^{-}}((x-3)^{2}-3)=(3-3)^{2}-3=-3.\n$$\n\nSo, ${lim}_{x\\to -{3}^{+}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to {3}^{-}}F(x).$\n\n- Statement IV is $\\text{false}$ since statement I is false.\n\n**Note:** The $6$-periodic extension of $F(x)$ to $x\\in R$ has the graph shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069003/assets/f4bfe80cbcc0821e93012a859ccc91b3614fa7db2df8e25399fbadc3ef7a3355.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069003/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e0ef6d55925293a63fd3c25a7345dea904c95e009d8872ee551c3b5128c1c58"} {"question" "q-342498" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069003/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "16a78fa02682c8710ae4fea2e334ad4fe71d7da89ab8b6f4e0fa5d230e3f7846"} {"question" "q-342498" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069003/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e0ef6d55925293a63fd3c25a7345dea904c95e009d8872ee551c3b5128c1c58"} {"question" "q-342498" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "False"] ["text" "True"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069003/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e0ef6d55925293a63fd3c25a7345dea904c95e009d8872ee551c3b5128c1c58"} {"question" "q-342498" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "False"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069003/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e0ef6d55925293a63fd3c25a7345dea904c95e009d8872ee551c3b5128c1c58"} {"question" "q-342498" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069003/state.json" "file_sha256" "1e0ef